Subject: Fuse a register VM `this` load into the property read that uses it

What this does
  When `load_this` is immediately followed by a `get_field` or `get_field2`
  whose receiver is that register, the pair becomes one `get_this_field` or
  `get_this_field2`. The fused instruction still writes `this` into its
  register, with the same non-strict coercion, and then reads the property
  through the same cache site. It is not formed across a branch target or a
  block start, and a `get_field` that already chains into the next read keeps
  that chain instead.

Why we need it
  Every `this.x` lowered to two dispatches. `load_this` was 12% of all
  executed register instructions on Octane deltablue and 7% on richards.

What it adds
  ROP_get_this_field, ROP_get_this_field2 - the fused opcodes, in the threaded
                                            handlers, the interpreter loop and
                                            the suspended-frame step table.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  Yes. It adds two register opcodes.

Notes
  Formed only under deferred reference counting, where a register store is a
  plain store.

